To solve this problem, we can use the proportions of the sides of the similar triangles:
\begin{align}
\frac{4}{XY} &= \frac{6}{BC} \\
XY &= \frac{6}{4} \cdot BC \\
XY &= 1.5 \cdot BC \\
XY + XZ &= 14 \text{ (since } XYZ \text{ is a triangle with side } XY \text{ and } XZ \text{)?) } \\
1.5 \cdot BC + XZ &= 14 \\
BC + XZ &= \frac{14}{1.5}  ~(\text{ since } XY + XZ = \text{side } ZY \text{ of } ABC) \\
BC + XZ &= 9
\end{align}

Since the triangles are similar, we have the following proportions of their corresponding angles:
\begin{align}
\frac{\angle A}{\angle X} &= \frac{\angle B}{\angle Y} = \frac{\angle C}{\angle Z} = k  ~(\text{ where } k \text{ is the scale factor}) \\
\Rightarrow \angle A + \angle B + \angle C &= k \cdot (\angle X + \angle Y + \angle Z) \\
180^\circ &= k \cdot 180^\circ \\
\Rightarrow \boxed{k &= 1}  ~(\text{ since the angle sum of a triangle is always 180 degrees})
\end{align}

So, $\angle B = 60^\circ$ forming a right triangle with $\angle A$ and $\angle C$. The other angle in the right triangle must be $90^\circ$.
From the right triangle:

\begin{align}
BC^2 + BC^2 (sin(60^\circ) + cos(60^\circ))^2 &= 9^2 \\
BC^2 (1 + 2sin(60^\circ)cos(60^\circ) + (sin(60^\circ)^2 + cos(60^\circ)^2)) &= 81 \\
BC^2 (1 + \sqrt{3}/2 * (1 - \sqrt{3}/2)) &= 81 \\
BC^2 (1 + \frac{2(1 - \sqrt{3})^2}{4}) &= 81 \\
BC^2 (1 + \frac{(1 - \sqrt{3})^2}{2}) &= 81 \\
BC^2 (2 - \sqrt{3} + \frac{3 - \sqrt{3}}{2}) &= 81 \\
BC^2 \cdot 2 - BC^2 \cdot \sqrt{3} + 6BC^2 - 6BC\sqrt{3} &= 81 \\
BC(\sqrt{3}BC - 6\sqrt{3} + 2\sqrt{3}BC - 6) &= 81 \\
\Rightarrow BC^2 - 12BC + 27 &= 0
\end{align}

To find $BC$:
\begin{align}
BC &= \frac{b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\
BC &= \frac{12 \pm \sqrt{(12)^2 - 4 \cdot 1 \cdot 27}}{2 \cdot 1} \\
BC &= \frac{12 \pm \sqrt{144 - 108}}{2} \\
BC &= \frac{12 \pm \sqrt{36}}{2} \\
BC &= \frac{12 \pm 6}{2}
\end{align}

\begin{align}
\Rightarrow BC &= \boxed{\frac{18}{2}} \\
&= \boxed{9}
\end{align}

Now we can find $XZ$:
\begin{align}
XZ &= 9 - BC \\
XZ &= 9 - 9 \\
XZ &= 9 - 9 + \sqrt{3} \cdot 9  ~(\text{using the hypotenuse-leg property in the right triangle } ABC) \\
XZ &= - 9 + 9 + \sqrt{3} \cdot 9 \\
XZ &= \boxed{9 \sqrt{3}}
\end{align}

Since opposite angles in similar triangles are congruent, and we know that $\angle A = 90^\circ$, then $\angle X = 90^\circ$. Therefore, $XZ = ZY$:
\begin{align}
ZY = \boxed{9 \sqrt{3}}
\end{align}

