- Now we can calculate the lateral surface area of the cylinder by taking the product of the circumference of the circle (which is $2\pi\radius$) and the height of the tube:
  \begin{align*}\text{lateral surface area} &= 2\pi\radius\height \\ &= 2\pi \times \boxed{ \text{3 centimeters} } \times \boxed{ \text{6 centimeters} } \\ &= 36 \pi \text{ square centimeters} \\ &= \boxed{ 36 \pi \unittext{ square centimeters} } \end{align*}

The lateral surface area is 36$\pi$ square centimeters. Now we want to find the volume of the tube. The formula for the volume of a cylinder is:

