\frac{2}{a} + \frac{1}{b} \geq \frac{2}{1 - 2(0)} + \frac{1}{0} = \infty
\end{align*}
However, we found a value that makes the numerator equal to zero (which would result in a minimum), so in fact the minimum value must be $\frac{1}{2}$. We saw that this value is approached from the right as $b$ approaches $-\frac{1}{2}$, so we'll use the value $b = -\frac{1}{2} + \epsilon$ (where $\epsilon > 0$) as a refined estimate to get a better numerical approximation of the minimum value:
