&= \frac{2}{1 + \epsilon} + \frac{-2}{1 - \epsilon}
\end{align*}
We want the minimum value, so we should underestimate $\min(\frac{2}{1 + \epsilon} + \frac{-2}{1 - \epsilon})$, which can be done by taking the smaller term:
