\end{align*}

Now, let's start constructing our sequence of binomial coefficients step-by-step:

\begin{align*}
\binom{14}{8} &= 3003 & \cdots & \text{(given)}
\\
\binom{13}{8} &= 3003 - \binom{14}{7} = 3003 - 3432 = -429 & \cdots & \text{(from the first set above)}
\\
\binom{12}{8} &= \binom{13}{8} + \binom{13}{7} = 3003 - 3432 + 3432 = 0 & \cdots & \text{(using the second set above)}
\\
\binom{12}{7} &= \binom{13}{7} - \binom{13}{6} & \cdots & \text{(from the computed $\binom{13}{6}$)}
\\
\binom{12}{7} &= 3432 - (\binom{13}{6} + \binom{13}{5}) & \cdots & \text{(using the first set to compute $\binom{13}{6}$) - note that this is equivalent to $\binom{12}{7} = 3432 - (3003 - 0) = 429$}
\\
\binom{12}{6} &= \binom{13}{6} - \binom{13}{5} = (3003 - 3432) - (3003 - 429) & \cdots & \text{(using the second set to compute $\binom{13}{6}$) - note that this is equivalent to $\binom{12}{6} = -2220$}
\\
\binom{11}{6} &= \binom{12}{6} + \binom{12}{5}
