\\
\binom{9}{5} &= \binom{10}{5} + \binom{10}{4}
\\
\vdots
\end{align*}

Now that we have the right sequence of binomial coefficients $\binom{i}{6}$ for suitable $0 \leq i \leq 15$, we can finally compute $\binom{15}{7}$ using our initial identity:

