a &= 3b
\end{align*}

Substitute the second equation into the first one:
\begin{align*}
2(3b) + 4b &= 5 \\
6b + 4b &= 5 \\
\boxed{10b} &= 5 \\
\text{ Solving for } b:  b &=\frac5{10} \\
\text{ Now, let's find } a: a &= 3b \\
      &= 3 \cdot \frac5{10} \\
      &= \boxed{\frac35}
\end{align*}
```

The final answer is \boxed{\frac35}

